# General Clean-Code Principles

- Make intent clear with descriptive names and small, focused methods.
- Remove duplication only when it represents one shared concept, not merely similar syntax.
- Keep state local; prefer immutable values and explicit ownership boundaries.
- Hide implementation details behind clear interfaces.
- Explain why in comments, and document exposed APIs.
- Keep changes scoped, and address technical debt only when directly relevant.
